      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "facts": [
        "Constrains leadership prestige, educational elitism, and claims that public success proves divine approval.",
        "Confidentiality protects privacy and fair process, but secrecy that hides danger, blocks reporting, destroys records, coordinates stories, or protects reputation is concealment.",
        "Requires data minimization, informed privacy limits, secure records, need-to-know access, lawful reporting, and transparent conflict-of-interest handling.",
        "Safe systems provide channels outside the accused person's authority, external options, conflict disclosure, timely triage, support, secure records, protection for complainants and witnesses, and remedies for retaliation.",
        "Rejects accused leaders receiving sole reports, selecting investigators, controlling communications, funding silence, threatening status, or retaliating through sermons, references, work, housing, aid, immigration, or social networks."
